.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
incompressible two-phase flow of immiscible fluids 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void csmp::Tutorial3_Example::Run ()\fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP

.PP
\fBExample\fP program that uses a mesh created with ANSYS-ICEM FE to build the \fBModel\fP and simulate incompressible two-phase flow using an IMPES (Implicit Pressure Explicit Saturation) or IMPIS (Implicit Pressure Implicit Saturation) approach based on the FE-FV scheme of CSMP\&. Output is written to Matlab files and individual groups are monitored

.PP
Tasks and exercises:

.PP
.IP "1." 4
Generate a 2D ANSYS mesh with a new geometry, check comphg\&.wikidot\&.com for a small how-to
.IP "2." 4
Compare results for implicit and explicit FV schemes and different timestepping\&.
.IP "3." 4
Compare results for homogeneous porous media to the analytical solution for the Buckley-Leverett problem
.IP "4." 4
Allow the user to define, at runtime (!), to choose between a different relperm models available in the two_phase directory
.IP "5." 4
Design and program a \fBVisitor\fP that computes the total mobility and phase mobilities using the kr-model that the user defines\&. Get together as a team to compare your visitors and generate a final version for the SVN (NB: The visitor should check that the results are within range and give error statements if the wrong variable placements are used or variables are not defined)
.IP "6." 4
Program a function that computes the capillary pressure at the element center as well as the derivative dpc/dS
.IP "7." 4
Program a diffusion algorithm, using the FE method, to solve the non-linear diffusion equation for the capillary pressure, i\&.e\&. phi dS/dt = div * ( lambda_star dpc/dS grad S )
.IP "8." 4
Compare simulations with and without capillary effects for explicit/implicit FV schemes and different time-steps\&. Analyse how the FV simulation of capillary spreading compares to your FE algorithm 
.PP

.PP
